# cinema crontab — installed by ../deploy.sh, edit it here not with crontab -e.
#
# Note that deploying does install this file, so a job added by hand with
# `crontab -e` would be removed by the next deploy. apply.sh --validate prints the
# diff against what is installed, so that loss is visible before it happens.

# Report cinema's own health to #homelab-logs whenever it happens to be awake.
#
# cinema is suspended most of the time, and cron does not replay jobs missed while
# suspended, so this fires four times a day *if* the machine is up. That is the
# honest semantic for this host: absence is normal, and the digester never alerts
# on cinema being quiet.
0 */6 * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/cinema/scripts/health-report.py

# Plex's cached plex.tv tokens go stale across a suspend and the owner then gets "no libraries"
# / "not authorized" until it restarts. cron has no resume hook and this host has no sudo, so
# every minute check whether the machine slept since the last run and restart Plex if so.
* * * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/cinema/scripts/plex-resume-restart.py >> /home/robby/plex-resume-restart.log 2>&1

# Sleep on its own overnight: every 15 minutes from midnight to 05:45, suspend once Plex has
# had no playback, no scan and nobody logged in for an hour (a wake or boot restarts the hour).
# Added 2026-10-11 after a power outage left cinema running for a day and a half.
*/15 0-5 * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/cinema/scripts/idle-suspend.py >> /home/robby/idle-suspend.log 2>&1
